.TH ZFSWATCHER-LEDCTL 8 "2026-11-22" "version 0.6.0"
.SH NAME
zfswatcher-ledctl \- control disk enclosure LEDs through sysfs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zfswatcher-ledctl
.IR pattern = device
.RI [ pattern = device ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zfswatcher-ledctl
is a small shell script which emulates a subset of
.BR ledctl (8).
It sets the fault and locate LEDs of disk slots in SES enclosures
using the
.B fault
and
.B locate
files in sysfs (below
.IR /sys/block/ disk /device/enclosure_device:* ).
Unlike
.BR ledctl (8)
it needs no root privileges as long as those files are writable by
the user, which the udev rule described below ensures for the
.B zfswatcher
group.
.PP
.BR zfswatcher (8)
can call this script as the LED control command in its configuration.
.SH ARGUMENTS
Each argument has the form
.IR pattern = device .
The
.I device
is a block device, for example
.IR /dev/disk/by-vdev/A1 .
Symbolic links are resolved; for device-mapper devices the first
underlying device is used.
The following patterns are supported:
.TP
.B normal
Switch both the fault and the locate LED off.
.TP
.B failure
Switch the fault LED on.
.TP
.B failure_off
Switch the fault LED off.
.TP
.B locate
Switch the locate LED on.
.TP
.B locate_off
Switch the locate LED off.
.PP
Other patterns are reported as "Unknown pattern name" and skipped.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/80-enclosure-zfswatcher.rules
udev rule which gives the group
.B zfswatcher
read and write access to
.IR /sys/class/enclosure .
Members of that group (including the
.B zfswatcher
daemon user) can therefore use the script.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The script always exits with 0, even if a device has no enclosure or a
sysfs file is missing or not writable.
Problems are printed to standard output ("Missing enclosure link for
device", "Missing file", "Permission denied"), as is the result of each
change ("SUCCESS" or "FAIL").
.SH EXAMPLES
Switch the locate LED of a disk on:
.PP
.RS
zfswatcher-ledctl locate=/dev/disk/by-vdev/A1
.RE
.PP
Switch the fault LED on:
.PP
.RS
zfswatcher-ledctl failure=/dev/disk/by-vdev/A1
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zfswatcher (8),
.BR ledctl (8)
